From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: per-sequence token mask for batched serving

Serving can ban a token set (llama_set_token_mask) for chosen sequences
(llama_set_seq_token_mask). The batched sampling path adds -inf to the
banned logits of those sequences' rows before the greedy argmax and before
backend sampler chains: a broadcast add when every output row is armed, a
per-row gather when only some are, nothing when none are.

Upstream: candidate.

